From 113f88707c0b077af86b92417772838a9c01ab79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aliaksei Ivanou <aliaksei.ivanou@innowise.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 18:44:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add --retry-failed command-line option

Parse --retry-failed N (unsigned, default 0) with the same number syntax as --shard-count, store it in ConfigData, and expose it through Config::retryFailed() and a non-pure IConfig::retryFailed() that returns 0, so existing IConfig implementations keep compiling. The runner does not use the value yet.

Tests: SelfTest 'Parsing retry-failed cli flag' (tagged [approvals] so the approval baselines stay unchanged) and CTests RetryFailed::Help and RetryFailed::CliError::*.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GunDRycct3rWzK5p7dpZxP
